Back-projection of COVID-19 deaths and estimation of instantaneous CFR

In order to estimate the probability of newly confirmed infected cases
who die later due to the infections on a given day, instantaneous case
fatality rate (iCFR) was used³⁸. One way to calculate iCFR is through a
non-parametric back-projection approach to retrospectively adjust the
time of death cases³⁹. This reduces the possible bias caused by
different time points between reporting of cases and deaths when
calculating the rate.

