          Descriptive analysis                We conducted an exploratory data analysis and provided summary statistics for weather conditions, air pollution and COVID-19 data in t
he UK. We observed diverse weather conditions and air pollution across the UK during the first lockdown period. Scotland and         England         experienced the minimum and max
imum temperatures (3.5 and         24.5         ◦        C), respectively, while temperature variation (mean          ±          standard deviation (SD):          14.6 ± 4.0   
      ) was greatest in England (Table S1). Wales had the most prolonged sunlight exposure, while Scotland experienced the least. In England and Wales, the median sunlight duration
 was almost         2                 -fold longer than that in         Northern Ireland        . The variation in humidity was similar across         all         the UK countries.
